WebCore on OpenSSL 4 (docs/w6.md W6b). W5d built OpenSSL 4.1, which makes
ASN1_STRING opaque and has EVP_PKEY_get0_RSA return a const key; WebCore
reads three ASN.1 strings' fields directly and keeps the key in a
non-const pointer, as OpenSSL 3 and BoringSSL allowed. Each read goes
through ASN1_STRING_type, _length and _get0_data instead, which every
OpenSSL since 1.1 has, and the key is const where it is held. Nothing
else changes: the same bytes are read in the same order.

